{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Em1fpvsJqAVJufhdxYXbXg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Verify the HMAC chain in audit-log.jsonl.\n3\t\n4\tPLAN-023 Phase B / ADR-055.\n5\t\n6\tWalks an audit-log.jsonl file (or stdin) from first to last entry,\n7\trecomputing the HMAC chain and comparing against the recorded ``hmac``\n8\tfield on each line. Exits 0 iff the chain is intact.\n9\t\n10\t## Exit codes\n11\t\n12\t- **0** — chain intact (or log empty / pre-v2.9 zone only).\n13\t- **1** — tamper detected (line-level report on stderr).\n14\t- **2** — audit-key file missing or unreadable.\n15\t- **3** — malformed JSONL line (distinct from tamper — operator action\n16\t  is \"recover the partial line\", not \"investigate tamper\").\n17\t- **4** — permission error on key or log.\n18\t\n19\t## Semantics\n20\t\n21\t1. Genesis ``prev_hmac = b'\\\\x00' * 32``.\n22\t2. Entry without ``hmac`` field in pre-v2.9 zone: tolerated (warning\n23\t   only). As soon as the first ``hmac``-bearing entry appears, the\n24\t   chain is ACTIVE for that file. Any subsequent entry WITHOUT\n25\t   ``hmac`` → tamper (transition-entry rule is one-way).\n26\t3. Entry with ``hmac`` field in CHAIN_ACTIVE state: recompute HMAC\n27\t   from (key, prev_hmac, entry_sans_hmac_and_hmac_error) and compare.\n28\t4. Chain resets ONLY on file boundary (log rotation). A single file\n29\t   does not carry multiple chains.\n30\t\n31\t## Non-goals\n32\t\n33\t- Does not read or rely on the sidecar ``audit-log.last-hmac`` file\n34\t  (the log itself is the source of truth for verification).\n35\t- Does not detect tail truncation (covered by external anchor,\n36\t  post-v1.6.0).\n37\t- Does not detect rollback to an older log+key snapshot pair.\n38\t\n39\t## The --strict-against-counter contract (FD-26, Owner decision S363-4)\n40\t\n41\tWith the flag, every outcome is one of the five exit codes above, carries a named\n42\treason, is exactly one JSON object on stdout under --json, and is never a traceback:\n43\t\n44\t- counter ABSENT: rc 0, with ``chain_length_source: \"absent\"`` visible (in the JSON,\n45\t  and on stderr without --json) because tail truncation was NOT checked;\n46\t- counter ILLEGIBLE (non-regular, undecodable, empty, not plain decimal digits):\n47\t  rc 3 ``chain_length_unreadable`` (rc 4 when the read is refused by permissions),\n48\t  never the 0 that ``audit_hmac.read_chain_length`` falls back to;\n49\t- an invalid --counter-override is judged before --help: rc 3\n50\t  ``counter_override_invalid``. Other argument errors are rc 3 ``invalid_arguments``:\n51\t  rc 2 means \"key missing\" in this contract, so strict cannot borrow argparse's rc;\n52\t- the log, from a file or from stdin, is decoded by one path with errors=\"strict\":\n53\t  rc 3 ``log_undecodable``. A log that is not a regular file is refused by fstat before\n54\t  any read (rc 3 ``log_not_regular``), so a FIFO cannot hang the walk.\n55\t\n56\tWithout the flag the CLI behaves as it did before this contract. In particular a\n57\tnon-regular log still blocks on read (``--log-file /dev/stdin`` is a supported form),\n58\tand a counter is not consulted at all.\n59\t\"\"\"\n60\t\n61\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n62\t\n63\timport argparse\n64\timport io\n65\timport json\n66\timport os\n67\timport re\n68\timport stat\n69\timport sys\n70\tfrom pathlib import Path\n71\tfrom typing import Any, Dict, Iterator, List, Optional, Tuple\n72\t\n73\t\n74\t_REPO_HOOKS = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"hooks\"\n75\tif str(_REPO_HOOKS) not in sys.path:\n76\t    sys.path.insert(0, str(_REPO_HOOKS))\n77\t\n78\tfrom _lib import audit_hmac  # noqa: E402\n79\tfrom _lib.audit_hmac import (  # noqa: E402\n80\t    AuditHmacError,\n81\t    GENESIS_PREV,\n82\t    HMAC_BYTES,\n83\t    HMAC_HEX_LEN,\n84\t    STATUS_INTACT,\n85\t    STATUS_KEY_MISSING,\n86\t    STATUS_MALFORMED,\n87\t    STATUS_PERM_ERROR,\n88\t    STATUS_TAMPER,\n89\t    VerifyResult,\n90\t    compute_entry_hmac,\n91\t    from_hex,\n92\t    verify_chain,\n93\t)\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t# Exit code constants\n97\tEXIT_INTACT = 0\n98\tEXIT_TAMPER = 1\n99\tEXIT_KEY_MISSING = 2\n100\tEXIT_MALFORMED = 3\n101\tEXIT_PERM = 4\n102\t\n103\t\n104\tdef _err(msg: str) -> None:\n105\t    sys.stderr.write(msg + \"\\n\")\n106\t\n107\t\n108\tclass _StrictFailure(Exception):\n109\t    \"\"\"One named outcome of the --strict-against-counter contract.\"\"\"\n110\t\n111\t    def __init__(self, code: int, status: str, reason: str) -> None:\n112\t        super().__init__(reason)\n113\t        self.code = code\n114\t        self.status = status\n115\t        self.reason = reason\n116\t\n117\t\n118\tdef _strict_emit(failure: _StrictFailure, json_output: bool) -> int:\n119\t    \"\"\"Report a strict failure on the channel the caller asked for; return its rc.\"\"\"\n120\t    if json_output:\n121\t        print(json.dumps({\n122\t            \"status\": failure.status,\n123\t            \"line\": 0,\n124\t            \"reason\": failure.reason,\n125\t            \"entry_ts\": None,\n126\t            \"entry_action\": None,\n127\t            \"expected_hmac\": None,\n128\t            \"actual_hmac\": None,\n129\t        }, separators=(\",\", \":\")))\n130\t    else:\n131\t        _err(\"error: \" + failure.reason)\n132\t    return failure.code\n133\t\n134\t\n135\tdef _refuse_json_constant(name: str) -> Any:\n136\t    \"\"\"parse_constant under strict: NaN/Infinity are not JSON, and a report that echoed\n137\t    one from an entry would not be valid JSON either.\"\"\"\n138\t    raise ValueError(\"non-standard JSON constant \" + name)\n139\t\n140\t\n141\tdef _read_key(key_file: Optional[Path]) -> bytes:\n142\t    \"\"\"Read and validate the audit-key.\n143\t\n144\t    If ``key_file`` is None, use :func:`audit_hmac.key_path`.\n145\t    \"\"\"\n146\t    p = key_file if key_file is not None else audit_hmac.key_path()\n147\t    if not p.exists():\n148\t        _err(\n149\t            \"error: audit-key not found at {p}; \"\n150\t            \"generate one by writing an audit entry, or pass --key-file\".format(p=p)\n151\t        )\n152\t        sys.exit(EXIT_KEY_MISSING)\n153\t    try:\n154\t        mode = p.stat().st_mode\n155\t    except OSError as e:\n156\t        _err(\"error: stat failed on {p}: {e}\".format(p=p, e=e))\n157\t        sys.exit(EXIT_PERM)\n158\t    if mode & 0o077 != 0:\n159\t        _err(\n160\t            \"error: unsafe perms on {p} (must be owner-only 0600)\".format(p=p)\n161\t        )\n162\t        sys.exit(EXIT_PERM)\n163\t    try:\n164\t        data = p.read_bytes()\n165\t    except OSError as e:\n166\t        _err(\"error: cannot read {p}: {e}\".format(p=p, e=e))\n167\t        sys.exit(EXIT_PERM)\n168\t    if len(data) != audit_hmac.KEY_BYTES:\n169\t        _err(\n170\t            \"error: {p} is {n} bytes (expected {k})\".format(\n171\t                p=p, n=len(data), k=audit_hmac.KEY_BYTES\n172\t            )\n173\t        )\n174\t        sys.exit(EXIT_PERM)\n175\t    return data\n176\t\n177\t\n178\tdef _format_report(\n179\t    status: str,\n180\t    line_num: int,\n181\t    entry: Optional[Dict[str, Any]],\n182\t    expected_hmac: Optional[str],\n183\t    actual_hmac: Optional[str],\n184\t    reason: str,\n185\t) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n186\t    \"\"\"Build structured JSON report for --json output.\"\"\"\n187\t    entry = entry if entry is not None else {}  # None: not about one line (line 0)\n188\t    return {\n189\t        \"status\": status,\n190\t        \"line\": line_num,\n191\t        \"reason\": reason,\n192\t        \"entry_ts\": entry.get(\"ts\"),\n193\t        \"entry_action\": entry.get(\"action\"),\n194\t        \"expected_hmac\": expected_hmac,\n195\t        \"actual_hmac\": actual_hmac,\n196\t    }\n197\t\n198\t\n199\tdef _emit_human_report(report: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n200\t    \"\"\"Pretty-print tamper report to stderr.\"\"\"\n201\t    sys.stderr.write(\n202\t        \"TAMPER DETECTED at line {line}\\n\".format(line=report[\"line\"])\n203\t    )\n204\t    sys.stderr.write(\n205\t        \"  entry_ts:      {ts}\\n\".format(ts=report.get(\"entry_ts\"))\n206\t    )\n207\t    sys.stderr.write(\n208\t        \"  entry_action:  {a}\\n\".format(a=report.get(\"entry_action\"))\n209\t    )\n210\t    sys.stderr.write(\"  reason:        {r}\\n\".format(r=report.get(\"reason\")))\n211\t    if report.get(\"expected_hmac\"):\n212\t        sys.stderr.write(\n213\t            \"  expected_hmac: {h}\\n\".format(h=report[\"expected_hmac\"])\n214\t        )\n215\t    if report.get(\"actual_hmac\"):\n216\t        sys.stderr.write(\n217\t            \"  actual_hmac:   {h}\\n\".format(h=report[\"actual_hmac\"])\n218\t        )\n219\t    sys.stderr.write(\n220\t        \"Chain broken. Do not trust entries >= line {n}.\\n\".format(\n221\t            n=report[\"line\"]\n222\t        )\n223\t    )\n224\t\n225\t\n226\tdef _emit_report(report, json_output: bool) -> None:\n227\t    \"\"\"Emit a tamper/malformed report either as JSON or human text.\"\"\"\n228\t    if json_output:\n229\t        print(json.dumps(report, separators=(\",\", \":\")))\n230\t    else:\n231\t        _emit_human_report(report)\n232\t\n233\t\n234\tdef _decode_entry(\n235\t    line_num: int, raw: str, strict_contract: bool = False,\n236\t) -> \"tuple[Optional[str], Optional[dict], Optional[int]]\":\n237\t    \"\"\"Parse raw line → (stripped, entry_dict or None, exit_code or None).\n238\t\n239\t    Returns ``(None, None, exit_code)`` on decode failure; returns\n240\t    ``(\"\", None, None)`` for blank lines; otherwise ``(stripped, entry, None)``.\n241\t    Under the strict contract a line that is not one JSON object raises\n242\t    :class:`_StrictFailure` instead, so that --json still gets its one object.\n243\t    \"\"\"\n244\t    stripped = raw.strip()\n245\t    if not stripped:\n246\t        return \"\", None, None\n247\t    if strict_contract:\n248\t        try:\n249\t            entry = json.loads(stripped, parse_constant=_refuse_json_constant)\n250\t        except (ValueError, RecursionError) as e:\n251\t            raise _StrictFailure(\n252\t                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n253\t                \"malformed_json_line: line {n}: {t}: {e}\".format(\n254\t                    n=line_num, t=type(e).__name__, e=str(e)[:200]),\n255\t            ) from e\n256\t        if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n257\t            raise _StrictFailure(\n258\t                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n259\t                \"malformed_json_line: line {n} is not a JSON object\".format(n=line_num),\n260\t            )\n261\t        return stripped, entry, None\n262\t    try:\n263\t        entry = json.loads(stripped)\n264\t    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n265\t        _err(\n266\t            \"error: line {n} is malformed JSON: {e}\".format(n=line_num, e=e)\n267\t        )\n268\t        return None, None, EXIT_MALFORMED\n269\t    if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n270\t        _err(\"error: line {n} is not a JSON object\".format(n=line_num))\n271\t        return None, None, EXIT_MALFORMED\n272\t    return stripped, entry, None\n273\t\n274\t\n275\tdef _classify_hmac_presence(\n276\t    state: str, entry: dict, line_num: int, json_output: bool,\n277\t) -> \"tuple[str, Any]\":\n278\t    \"\"\"Handle the hmac-missing vs. hmac-present fork.\n279\t\n280\t    Returns ``(status, payload)`` where status is one of:\n281\t      - ``\"pre_v29\"`` — pre-v2.9 entry, skip with counter bump\n282\t      - ``\"transition\"`` — violation: hmac-bearing → hmac-less, exit tamper\n283\t      - ``\"malformed\"`` — hmac field wrong type/length, exit malformed\n284\t      - ``\"ok\"`` — payload is the validated hmac_hex string\n285\t    \"\"\"\n286\t    hmac_hex = entry.get(\"hmac\")\n287\t    if hmac_hex is None:\n288\t        if state == \"CHAIN_START\":\n289\t            return \"pre_v29\", None\n290\t        report = _format_report(\n291\t            \"tamper\", line_num, entry, None, None,\n292\t            \"transition_violation: hmac-bearing entry followed by \"\n293\t            \"hmac-less entry (one-way rule)\",\n294\t        )\n295\t        _emit_report(report, json_output)\n296\t        return \"transition\", EXIT_TAMPER\n297\t\n298\t    if not isinstance(hmac_hex, str) or len(hmac_hex) != HMAC_HEX_LEN:\n299\t        report = _format_report(\n300\t            \"malformed\", line_num, entry, None, str(hmac_hex),\n301\t            \"hmac_field_malformed: not 64 hex chars\",\n302\t        )\n303\t        _emit_report(report, json_output)\n304\t        return \"malformed\", EXIT_MALFORMED\n305\t\n306\t    return \"ok\", hmac_hex\n307\t\n308\t\n309\tdef _verify_entry_hmac(\n310\t    key: bytes,\n311\t    prev_hmac: bytes,\n312\t    entry: dict,\n313\t    hmac_hex: str,\n314\t    line_num: int,\n315\t    json_output: bool,\n316\t    strict_contract: bool = False,\n317\t) -> \"tuple[Optional[bytes], Optional[int]]\":\n318\t    \"\"\"Recompute entry HMAC + constant-time compare against recorded.\n319\t\n320\t    Returns ``(new_prev_hmac, exit_code)``. On success returns\n321\t    ``(actual_bytes, None)``; on failure returns ``(None, exit_code)``.\n322\t    \"\"\"\n323\t    entry_sans = {\n324\t        k: v for k, v in entry.items()\n325\t        if k != \"hmac\" and k != \"hmac_error\"\n326\t    }\n327\t    try:\n328\t        expected = compute_entry_hmac(key, prev_hmac, entry_sans)\n329\t    except AuditHmacError as e:\n330\t        if strict_contract:\n331\t            raise _StrictFailure(\n332\t                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n333\t                \"hmac_compute_failed: line {n}: {e}\".format(n=line_num, e=e),\n334\t            ) from e\n335\t        _err(\n336\t            \"error: HMAC compute failed at line {n}: {e}\".format(\n337\t                n=line_num, e=e\n338\t            )\n339\t        )\n340\t        return None, EXIT_MALFORMED\n341\t\n342\t    try:\n343\t        actual = from_hex(hmac_hex)\n344\t    except AuditHmacError as e:\n345\t        if strict_contract:\n346\t            raise _StrictFailure(\n347\t                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n348\t                \"hmac_field_unparseable: line {n}: {e}\".format(n=line_num, e=e),\n349\t            ) from e\n350\t        _err(\n351\t            \"error: hmac field not parseable at line {n}: {e}\".format(\n352\t                n=line_num, e=e\n353\t            )\n354\t        )\n355\t        return None, EXIT_MALFORMED\n356\t\n357\t    import hmac as _h\n358\t    if not _h.compare_digest(expected, actual):\n359\t        report = _format_report(\n360\t            \"tamper\", line_num, entry,\n361\t            expected.hex(), hmac_hex,\n362\t            \"hmac_mismatch: recomputed does not match recorded\",\n363\t        )\n364\t        _emit_report(report, json_output)\n365\t        return None, EXIT_TAMPER\n366\t\n367\t    return actual, None\n368\t\n369\t\n370\tdef verify(\n371\t    log_lines,\n372\t    key: bytes,\n373\t    since: int = 1,\n374\t    json_output: bool = False,\n375\t    verbose: bool = False,\n376\t    enforce_marker_if_manifest: bool = True,\n377\t    log_dir: Optional[Path] = None,\n378\t    strict_against_counter: bool = False,\n379\t    counter_override: Optional[int] = None,\n380\t    chain_length_source: Optional[str] = None,\n381\t) -> int:\n382\t    \"\"\"Walk lines; return an exit code.\n383\t\n384\t    ``chain_length_source`` is set only by :func:`_main_strict` and turns on the strict\n385\t    contract of the module docstring: ``sidecar``, ``override`` or ``absent``.\n386\t\n387\t    ``log_lines`` is an iterable of (line_num, raw_line) tuples.\n388\t    ``since`` is 1-indexed starting line.\n389\t\n390\t    Chain state machine:\n391\t      CHAIN_START — no hmac seen yet (pre-v2.9 zone).\n392\t      CHAIN_ACTIVE — at least one hmac seen; prev_hmac tracked.\n393\t\n394\t    PLAN-112-FOLLOWUP-hmac-tamper-fix Wave B.3 / ADR-055-AMEND-2:\n395\t    If ``enforce_marker_if_manifest=True`` AND the\n396\t    ``audit-log.rotation-manifest.json`` sidecar exists, line 1 of the\n397\t    log MUST be an entry with ``action == \"chain_reset_marker\"``;\n398\t    otherwise STATUS_TAMPER. Verifier uses LOCAL semantics (line 1\n399\t    inspection + sidecar presence); does NOT walk archives.\n400\t    \"\"\"\n401\t    # AC12 enforcement: manifest-mode marker check on line 1. Read manifest\n402\t    # from log's SAME directory (NOT _audit_dir_from_env) so test envs with\n403\t    # custom log paths don't inherit production manifest state.\n404\t    manifest_present = False\n405\t    if enforce_marker_if_manifest and log_dir is not None:\n406\t        try:\n407\t            manifest_path = log_dir / audit_hmac.ROTATION_MANIFEST_FILENAME\n408\t            manifest_present = manifest_path.exists()\n409\t        except Exception:\n410\t            manifest_present = False\n411\t\n412\t    state = \"CHAIN_START\"\n413\t    prev_hmac = GENESIS_PREV\n414\t    verified_count = 0\n415\t    pre_v29_count = 0\n416\t    first_chain_line_checked = False\n417\t    strict_contract = chain_length_source is not None\n418\t\n419\t    for line_num, raw in log_lines:\n420\t        if line_num < since:\n421\t            continue\n422\t\n423\t        stripped, entry, exit_code = _decode_entry(line_num, raw, strict_contract)\n424\t        if exit_code is not None:\n425\t            return exit_code\n426\t        if not stripped:\n427\t            continue\n428\t        assert entry is not None\n429\t\n430\t        status, payload = _classify_hmac_presence(\n431\t            state, entry, line_num, json_output\n432\t        )\n433\t        if status == \"pre_v29\":\n434\t            pre_v29_count += 1\n435\t            continue\n436\t        if status in (\"transition\", \"malformed\"):\n437\t            return payload  # type: ignore[return-value]\n438\t\n439\t        hmac_hex = payload  # \"ok\" path\n440\t        assert isinstance(hmac_hex, str)\n441\t\n442\t        if state == \"CHAIN_START\":\n443\t            state = \"CHAIN_ACTIVE\"\n444\t            prev_hmac = GENESIS_PREV\n445\t\n446\t        # AC12 enforcement: if rotation-manifest sidecar present, FIRST\n447\t        # chain-active entry MUST be chain_reset_marker. Non-marker line 1\n448\t        # in marker-required mode = STATUS_TAMPER per ADR-055-AMEND-2.\n449\t        if (enforce_marker_if_manifest and manifest_present\n450\t                and not first_chain_line_checked):\n451\t            first_chain_line_checked = True\n452\t            if entry.get(\"action\") != \"chain_reset_marker\":\n453\t                report = _format_report(\n454\t                    \"tamper\", line_num, entry, None, None,\n455\t                    \"marker_required_but_absent: audit-log.rotation-manifest.json \"\n456\t                    \"present but line 1 action is not chain_reset_marker per \"\n457\t                    \"ADR-055-AMEND-2\",\n458\t                )\n459\t                _emit_report(report, json_output)\n460\t                return EXIT_TAMPER\n461\t\n462\t        new_prev, exit_code = _verify_entry_hmac(\n463\t            key, prev_hmac, entry, hmac_hex, line_num, json_output, strict_contract\n464\t        )\n465\t        if exit_code is not None:\n466\t            return exit_code\n467\t        assert new_prev is not None\n468\t        prev_hmac = new_prev\n469\t        verified_count += 1\n470\t\n471\t    # PLAN-118 AC-B9-ii — strict-against-counter tail-truncation detection.\n472\t    # The persisted ``audit-log.chain-length`` counter is the monotonic\n473\t    # number of HMAC-bearing entries ever written (incremented under the\n474\t    # same FileLock as the entry itself). If the walker saw FEWER\n475\t    # HMAC-bearing entries than the counter says, the chain tail has\n476\t    # been truncated even though the surviving prefix verifies clean.\n477\t    # Flag as STATUS_TAMPER with reason=chain_length_truncation.\n478\t    if strict_against_counter:\n479\t        try:\n480\t            expected_length = (\n481\t                counter_override if counter_override is not None\n482\t                else audit_hmac.read_chain_length()\n483\t            )\n484\t        except Exception as e:\n485\t            report = _format_report(\n486\t                \"tamper\", 0, None, None, None,\n487\t                f\"chain_length_read_failed: {type(e).__name__}: {e}\",\n488\t            )\n489\t            _emit_report(report, json_output)\n490\t            return EXIT_TAMPER\n491\t        if verified_count < expected_length:\n492\t            report = _format_report(\n493\t                \"tamper\", 0, None, None, None,\n494\t                \"chain_length_truncation: walker counted {v} HMAC-bearing \"\n495\t                \"entries, persisted counter says {n}\".format(\n496\t                    v=verified_count, n=expected_length\n497\t                ),\n498\t            )\n499\t            report[\"verified_count\"] = verified_count\n500\t            report[\"expected_length\"] = expected_length\n501\t            _emit_report(report, json_output)\n502\t            return EXIT_TAMPER\n503\t\n504\t    summary: Dict[str, Any] = {\n505\t        \"status\": \"intact\",\n506\t        \"verified_count\": verified_count,\n507\t        \"pre_v29_count\": pre_v29_count,\n508\t    }\n509\t    if chain_length_source is not None:\n510\t        summary[\"chain_length_source\"] = chain_length_source\n511\t        if not json_output and chain_length_source == \"absent\":\n512\t            _err(\n513\t                \"warning: chain_length_source=absent: no chain-length counter, \"\n514\t                \"tail truncation NOT checked\"\n515\t            )\n516\t    if json_output:\n517\t        print(json.dumps(summary, separators=(\",\", \":\")))\n518\t    elif verbose:\n519\t        sys.stderr.write(\n520\t            \"OK: chain intact. verified={v} pre_v29={p}\\n\".format(\n521\t                v=verified_count, p=pre_v29_count\n522\t            )\n523\t        )\n524\t    return EXIT_INTACT\n525\t\n526\t\n527\tdef _iter_lines(log_path: Optional[Path]) -> \"Iterator[tuple[int, str]]\":\n528\t    \"\"\"Yield ``(line_num, raw_line)`` pairs from file or stdin.\"\"\"\n529\t    if log_path is None:\n530\t        for i, raw in enumerate(sys.stdin, start=1):\n531\t            yield (i, raw)\n532\t        return\n533\t    if not log_path.exists():\n534\t        _err(\"error: log file not found: {p}\".format(p=log_path))\n535\t        sys.exit(EXIT_MALFORMED)\n536\t    with log_path.open(\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n537\t        for i, raw in enumerate(f, start=1):\n538\t            yield (i, raw)\n539\t\n540\t\n541\t_COUNTER_RE = re.compile(r\"[0-9]{1,32}\")\n542\t_NONBLOCK_READ = os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NONBLOCK | getattr(os, \"O_CLOEXEC\", 0)\n543\t\n544\t\n545\tdef _open_regular_strict(path: Path, what: str, unreadable: str) -> \"io.BufferedReader\":\n546\t    \"\"\"Open without blocking; refuse by fstat what is not a regular file.\n547\t\n548\t    The check and the read act on the same descriptor. O_NONBLOCK is why a FIFO with\n549\t    no writer returns here instead of hanging on the open.\n550\t    \"\"\"\n551\t    try:\n552\t        fd = os.open(str(path), _NONBLOCK_READ)\n553\t    except PermissionError as e:\n554\t        raise _StrictFailure(\n555\t            EXIT_PERM, STATUS_PERM_ERROR,\n556\t            \"{w}: cannot read {p}: {e}\".format(w=unreadable, p=path, e=e),\n557\t        ) from e\n558\t    except OSError as e:\n559\t        raise _StrictFailure(\n560\t            EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n561\t            \"{w}: cannot open {p}: {t}: {e}\".format(\n562\t                w=unreadable, p=path, t=type(e).__name__, e=e),\n563\t        ) from e\n564\t    if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(fd).st_mode):\n565\t        os.close(fd)\n566\t        raise _StrictFailure(\n567\t            EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n568\t            \"{w}: {what} {p} is not a regular file\".format(w=unreadable, what=what, p=path),\n569\t        )\n570\t    return os.fdopen(fd, \"rb\")\n571\t\n572\t\n573\tdef _expected_length_strict(counter_override: Optional[int]) -> Tuple[int, str]:\n574\t    \"\"\"``(expected length, source)``. Unlike ``audit_hmac.read_chain_length``, an\n575\t    illegible counter is an error (S363-4): only real absence is allowed through.\"\"\"\n576\t    if counter_override is not None:\n577\t        return counter_override, \"override\"\n578\t    path = audit_hmac.chain_length_path()\n579\t    try:\n580\t        os.lstat(str(path))\n581\t    except FileNotFoundError:\n582\t        return 0, \"absent\"\n583\t    except OSError as e:\n584\t        raise _StrictFailure(\n585\t            EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n586\t            \"chain_length_unreadable: cannot stat {p}: {e}\".format(p=path, e=e),\n587\t        ) from e\n588\t    with _open_regular_strict(path, \"counter\", \"chain_length_unreadable\") as stream:\n589\t        raw = stream.read(64)\n590\t    text = raw.decode(\"ascii\", \"replace\").strip(\" \\t\\r\\n\")\n591\t    if _COUNTER_RE.fullmatch(text) is None:\n592\t        raise _StrictFailure(\n593\t            EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n594\t            \"chain_length_unreadable: {p} does not hold a plain decimal count\".format(p=path),\n595\t        )\n596\t    return int(text), \"sidecar\"\n597\t\n598\t\n599\tdef _read_key_strict(key_file: Optional[Path]) -> bytes:\n600\t    \"\"\":func:`_read_key` with its exits and OS errors mapped to named failures.\"\"\"\n601\t    try:\n602\t        return _read_key(key_file)\n603\t    except SystemExit as e:\n604\t        if e.code == EXIT_KEY_MISSING:\n605\t            raise _StrictFailure(EXIT_KEY_MISSING, STATUS_KEY_MISSING, \"key_missing\") from e\n606\t        raise _StrictFailure(EXIT_PERM, STATUS_PERM_ERROR, \"key_unusable\") from e\n607\t    except OSError as e:\n608\t        raise _StrictFailure(\n609\t            EXIT_PERM, STATUS_PERM_ERROR, \"key_unusable: {e}\".format(e=e)\n610\t        ) from e\n611\t\n612\t\n613\tdef _open_log_strict(log_path: Optional[Path]) -> \"io.TextIOWrapper\":\n614\t    \"\"\"One decoding path for file and stdin, so the same bytes get the same verdict.\"\"\"\n615\t    if log_path is None:\n616\t        return io.TextIOWrapper(sys.stdin.buffer, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n617\t    try:\n618\t        os.lstat(str(log_path))\n619\t    except FileNotFoundError as e:\n620\t        raise _StrictFailure(\n621\t            EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n622\t            \"log_not_found: {p}\".format(p=log_path),\n623\t        ) from e\n624\t    except OSError:\n625\t        pass  # the open below names it\n626\t    binary = _open_regular_strict(log_path, \"log\", \"log_not_regular\")\n627\t    return io.TextIOWrapper(binary, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n628\t\n629\t\n630\tdef _main_strict(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n631\t    \"\"\"The --strict-against-counter contract of the module docstring.\"\"\"\n632\t    try:\n633\t        log_path = _resolve_log_path(args)\n634\t        if log_path is _LOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED:\n635\t            raise _StrictFailure(\n636\t                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n637\t                \"log_unresolved: cannot resolve default audit-log path; pass --log-file\",\n638\t            )\n639\t        key = _read_key_strict(args.key_file)\n640\t        expected, source = _expected_length_strict(args.counter_override)\n641\t        stream = _open_log_strict(log_path)\n642\t        try:\n643\t            return verify(\n644\t                enumerate(stream, start=1),\n645\t                key,\n646\t                since=args.since,\n647\t                json_output=args.json,\n648\t                verbose=args.verbose,\n649\t                log_dir=log_path.parent if log_path is not None else None,\n650\t                strict_against_counter=True,\n651\t                counter_override=expected,\n652\t                chain_length_source=source,\n653\t            )\n654\t        finally:\n655\t            stream.close()\n656\t    except _StrictFailure as failure:\n657\t        return _strict_emit(failure, args.json)\n658\t    except UnicodeError as e:\n659\t        return _strict_emit(\n660\t            _StrictFailure(\n661\t                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n662\t                \"log_undecodable: {t}: {e}\".format(t=type(e).__name__, e=str(e)[:200]),\n663\t            ),\n664\t            args.json,\n665\t        )\n666\t    except Exception as e:  # the CLI's boundary: named and fail-closed, no traceback\n667\t        return _strict_emit(\n668\t            _StrictFailure(\n669\t                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n670\t                \"internal_error: {t}: {e}\".format(t=type(e).__name__, e=str(e)[:200]),\n671\t            ),\n672\t            args.json,\n673\t        )\n674\t\n675\t\n676\tclass _PreScanFailed(Exception):\n677\t    \"\"\"The lenient pre-scan could not read the argv.\"\"\"\n678\t\n679\t\n680\tclass _PreScanParser(argparse.ArgumentParser):\n681\t    \"\"\"Only learns whether this is a strict run; never reports anything itself.\"\"\"\n682\t\n683\t    def error(self, message: str) -> Any:\n684\t        raise _PreScanFailed(message)\n685\t\n686\t\n687\tclass _ContractParser(argparse.ArgumentParser):\n688\t    \"\"\"argparse, except that under strict an argument error is a named rc 3.\"\"\"\n689\t\n690\t    strict_json: Optional[bool] = None  # None: not strict, stock behaviour\n691\t\n692\t    def error(self, message: str) -> Any:\n693\t        if self.strict_json is None:\n694\t            super().error(message)\n695\t        raise SystemExit(\n696\t            _strict_emit(\n697\t                _StrictFailure(\n698\t                    EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n699\t                    \"invalid_arguments: \" + message,\n700\t                ),\n701\t                self.strict_json,\n702\t            )\n703\t        )\n704\t\n705\t\n706\tdef _strict_prescan(argv: List[str]) -> Tuple[bool, bool, Optional[str]]:\n707\t    \"\"\"``(strict, json, raw override)``, before argparse validates or prints help.\n708\t\n709\t    The same options as the real parser (abbreviations stay as ambiguous as they are\n710\t    there) without its value types. An argv the scan cannot read falls back to looking\n711\t    for the two flags by token.\n712\t    \"\"\"\n713\t    pre = _add_arguments(_PreScanParser(add_help=False), lenient=True)\n714\t    try:\n715\t        known, _ = pre.parse_known_args(argv)\n716\t    except _PreScanFailed:\n717\t        def has(flag: str, floor: str) -> bool:\n718\t            return any(t.startswith(floor) and flag.startswith(t) for t in argv)\n719\t        return (\n720\t            has(\"--strict-against-counter\", \"--str\"),\n721\t            has(\"--json\", \"--j\"),\n722\t            None,\n723\t        )\n724\t    return known.strict_against_counter, known.json, known.counter_override\n725\t\n726\t\n727\t_LOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED = Path(\"/nonexistent/ceo-audit-log-unresolved\")\n728\t\n729\t\n730\tdef _resolve_log_path(args: argparse.Namespace) -> Optional[Path]:\n731\t    \"\"\"The log path of ``args``: None means stdin. :data:`_LOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED` means\n732\t    the default directory could not be resolved.\"\"\"\n733\t    if args.stdin or (args.log_file is not None and str(args.log_file) == \"-\"):\n734\t        return None\n735\t    if args.log_file is not None:\n736\t        return args.log_file\n737\t    env_log = os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH\")\n738\t    if env_log:\n739\t        return Path(env_log)\n740\t    # Default: sibling of audit-key resolution.\n741\t    try:\n742\t        default_dir = audit_hmac._audit_dir_from_env()\n743\t    except Exception:\n744\t        return _LOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED\n745\t    return default_dir / \"audit-log.jsonl\"\n746\t\n747\t\n748\tdef _add_arguments(parser: Any, lenient: bool = False) -> Any:\n749\t    \"\"\"Declare the CLI. ``lenient`` leaves the two int values unconverted (pre-scan).\"\"\"\n750\t    int_type = str if lenient else int\n751\t    parser.add_argument(\n752\t        \"--log-file\",\n753\t        type=Path,\n754\t        default=None,\n755\t        help=\"Path to audit-log.jsonl (default: resolved via env / stdin)\",\n756\t    )\n757\t    parser.add_argument(\n758\t        \"--key-file\",\n759\t        type=Path,\n760\t        default=None,\n761\t        help=\"Path to audit-key (default: resolved via env)\",\n762\t    )\n763\t    parser.add_argument(\n764\t        \"--since\",\n765\t        type=int_type,\n766\t        default=1,\n767\t        help=\"1-indexed starting line (default: 1 = verify from genesis)\",\n768\t    )\n769\t    parser.add_argument(\n770\t        \"--json\",\n771\t        action=\"store_true\",\n772\t        help=\"Emit structured JSON report to stdout\",\n773\t    )\n774\t    parser.add_argument(\n775\t        \"--verbose\",\n776\t        action=\"store_true\",\n777\t        help=\"Print 'OK' summary on success (default: silent success)\",\n778\t    )\n779\t    parser.add_argument(\n780\t        \"--stdin\",\n781\t        action=\"store_true\",\n782\t        help=\"Read log from stdin (equivalent to --log-file -)\",\n783\t    )\n784\t    parser.add_argument(\n785\t        \"--strict-against-counter\",\n786\t        action=\"store_true\",\n787\t        help=(\n788\t            \"PLAN-118 AC-B9 — additionally enforce \"\n789\t            \"verified_count >= audit-log.chain-length (tail-truncation \"\n790\t            \"detection). Without this flag, a truncated tail whose \"\n791\t            \"surviving prefix verifies clean would be reported intact.\"\n792\t        ),\n793\t    )\n794\t    parser.add_argument(\n795\t        \"--counter-override\",\n796\t        type=int_type,\n797\t        default=None,\n798\t        help=(\n799\t            \"Test/forensic-only: override the persisted \"\n800\t            \"audit-log.chain-length counter (paired with \"\n801\t            \"--strict-against-counter). Default reads the on-disk sidecar.\"\n802\t        ),\n803\t    )\n804\t    return parser\n805\t\n806\t\n807\tdef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n808\t    \"\"\"CLI entrypoint — verify an audit-log HMAC chain end-to-end.\"\"\"\n809\t    args_in = list(sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv)\n810\t    strict, strict_json, raw_override = _strict_prescan(args_in)\n811\t    if strict and raw_override is not None and _COUNTER_RE.fullmatch(raw_override) is None:\n812\t        return _strict_emit(\n813\t            _StrictFailure(\n814\t                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n815\t                \"counter_override_invalid: expected plain decimal digits\",\n816\t            ),\n817\t            strict_json,\n818\t        )\n819\t    parser = _ContractParser(\n820\t        description=\"Verify the HMAC chain in audit-log.jsonl.\",\n821\t        epilog=\"Exit 0=intact, 1=tamper, 2=key missing, 3=malformed, 4=perm.\",\n822\t    )\n823\t    if strict:\n824\t        parser.strict_json = strict_json\n825\t    args = _add_arguments(parser).parse_args(args_in)\n826\t    if args.strict_against_counter:\n827\t        return _main_strict(args)\n828\t\n829\t    # Resolve log path.\n830\t    log_path = _resolve_log_path(args)\n831\t    if log_path is _LOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED:\n832\t        _err(\"error: cannot resolve default audit-log path; \"\n833\t             \"pass --log-file\")\n834\t        return EXIT_MALFORMED\n835\t\n836\t    # Read key.\n837\t    try:\n838\t        key = _read_key(args.key_file)\n839\t    except SystemExit:\n840\t        raise\n841\t\n842\t    return verify(\n843\t        _iter_lines(log_path),\n844\t        key,\n845\t        since=args.since,\n846\t        json_output=args.json,\n847\t        verbose=args.verbose,\n848\t        log_dir=log_path.parent if hasattr(log_path, \"parent\") else None,\n849\t    )\n850\t\n851\t\n852\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n853\t    sys.exit(main())\n854\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"686fe0c6-c9dd-4361-bad4-fda29b25a7f7","uuid":"9e88e279-2f94-49b3-9acb-a5aa3e78cba6","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:38:33.420Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/scripts/audit-verify-chain.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Verify the HMAC chain in audit-log.jsonl.\n\nPLAN-023 Phase B / ADR-055.\n\nWalks an audit-log.jsonl file (or stdin) from first to last entry,\nrecomputing the HMAC chain and comparing against the recorded ``hmac``\nfield on each line. Exits 0 iff the chain is intact.\n\n## Exit codes\n\n- **0** — chain intact (or log empty / pre-v2.9 zone only).\n- **1** — tamper detected (line-level report on stderr).\n- **2** — audit-key file missing or unreadable.\n- **3** — malformed JSONL line (distinct from tamper — operator action\n  is \"recover the partial line\", not \"investigate tamper\").\n- **4** — permission error on key or log.\n\n## Semantics\n\n1. Genesis ``prev_hmac = b'\\\\x00' * 32``.\n2. Entry without ``hmac`` field in pre-v2.9 zone: tolerated (warning\n   only). As soon as the first ``hmac``-bearing entry appears, the\n   chain is ACTIVE for that file. Any subsequent entry WITHOUT\n   ``hmac`` → tamper (transition-entry rule is one-way).\n3. Entry with ``hmac`` field in CHAIN_ACTIVE state: recompute HMAC\n   from (key, prev_hmac, entry_sans_hmac_and_hmac_error) and compare.\n4. Chain resets ONLY on file boundary (log rotation). A single file\n   does not carry multiple chains.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Does not read or rely on the sidecar ``audit-log.last-hmac`` file\n  (the log itself is the source of truth for verification).\n- Does not detect tail truncation (covered by external anchor,\n  post-v1.6.0).\n- Does not detect rollback to an older log+key snapshot pair.\n\n## The --strict-against-counter contract (FD-26, Owner decision S363-4)\n\nWith the flag, every outcome is one of the five exit codes above, carries a named\nreason, is exactly one JSON object on stdout under --json, and is never a traceback:\n\n- counter ABSENT: rc 0, with ``chain_length_source: \"absent\"`` visible (in the JSON,\n  and on stderr without --json) because tail truncation was NOT checked;\n- counter ILLEGIBLE (non-regular, undecodable, empty, not plain decimal digits):\n  rc 3 ``chain_length_unreadable`` (rc 4 when the read is refused by permissions),\n  never the 0 that ``audit_hmac.read_chain_length`` falls back to;\n- an invalid --counter-override is judged before --help: rc 3\n  ``counter_override_invalid``. Other argument errors are rc 3 ``invalid_arguments``:\n  rc 2 means \"key missing\" in this contract, so strict cannot borrow argparse's rc;\n- the log, from a file or from stdin, is decoded by one path with errors=\"strict\":\n  rc 3 ``log_undecodable``. A log that is not a regular file is refused by fstat before\n  any read (rc 3 ``log_not_regular``), so a FIFO cannot hang the walk.\n\nWithout the flag the CLI behaves as it did before this contract. In particular a\nnon-regular log still blocks on read (``--log-file /dev/stdin`` is a supported form),\nand a counter is not consulted at all.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport io\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Iterator, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n\n_REPO_HOOKS = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"hooks\"\nif str(_REPO_HOOKS) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_REPO_HOOKS))\n\nfrom _lib import audit_hmac  # noqa: E402\nfrom _lib.audit_hmac import (  # noqa: E402\n    AuditHmacError,\n    GENESIS_PREV,\n    HMAC_BYTES,\n    HMAC_HEX_LEN,\n    STATUS_INTACT,\n    STATUS_KEY_MISSING,\n    STATUS_MALFORMED,\n    STATUS_PERM_ERROR,\n    STATUS_TAMPER,\n    VerifyResult,\n    compute_entry_hmac,\n    from_hex,\n    verify_chain,\n)\n\n\n# Exit code constants\nEXIT_INTACT = 0\nEXIT_TAMPER = 1\nEXIT_KEY_MISSING = 2\nEXIT_MALFORMED = 3\nEXIT_PERM = 4\n\n\ndef _err(msg: str) -> None:\n    sys.stderr.write(msg + \"\\n\")\n\n\nclass _StrictFailure(Exception):\n    \"\"\"One named outcome of the --strict-against-counter contract.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, code: int, status: str, reason: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(reason)\n        self.code = code\n        self.status = status\n        self.reason = reason\n\n\ndef _strict_emit(failure: _StrictFailure, json_output: bool) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Report a strict failure on the channel the caller asked for; return its rc.\"\"\"\n    if json_output:\n        print(json.dumps({\n            \"status\": failure.status,\n            \"line\": 0,\n            \"reason\": failure.reason,\n            \"entry_ts\": None,\n            \"entry_action\": None,\n            \"expected_hmac\": None,\n            \"actual_hmac\": None,\n        }, separators=(\",\", \":\")))\n    else:\n        _err(\"error: \" + failure.reason)\n    return failure.code\n\n\ndef _refuse_json_constant(name: str) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"parse_constant under strict: NaN/Infinity are not JSON, and a report that echoed\n    one from an entry would not be valid JSON either.\"\"\"\n    raise ValueError(\"non-standard JSON constant \" + name)\n\n\ndef _read_key(key_file: Optional[Path]) -> bytes:\n    \"\"\"Read and validate the audit-key.\n\n    If ``key_file`` is None, use :func:`audit_hmac.key_path`.\n    \"\"\"\n    p = key_file if key_file is not None else audit_hmac.key_path()\n    if not p.exists():\n        _err(\n            \"error: audit-key not found at {p}; \"\n            \"generate one by writing an audit entry, or pass --key-file\".format(p=p)\n        )\n        sys.exit(EXIT_KEY_MISSING)\n    try:\n        mode = p.stat().st_mode\n    except OSError as e:\n        _err(\"error: stat failed on {p}: {e}\".format(p=p, e=e))\n        sys.exit(EXIT_PERM)\n    if mode & 0o077 != 0:\n        _err(\n            \"error: unsafe perms on {p} (must be owner-only 0600)\".format(p=p)\n        )\n        sys.exit(EXIT_PERM)\n    try:\n        data = p.read_bytes()\n    except OSError as e:\n        _err(\"error: cannot read {p}: {e}\".format(p=p, e=e))\n        sys.exit(EXIT_PERM)\n    if len(data) != audit_hmac.KEY_BYTES:\n        _err(\n            \"error: {p} is {n} bytes (expected {k})\".format(\n                p=p, n=len(data), k=audit_hmac.KEY_BYTES\n            )\n        )\n        sys.exit(EXIT_PERM)\n    return data\n\n\ndef _format_report(\n    status: str,\n    line_num: int,\n    entry: Optional[Dict[str, Any]],\n    expected_hmac: Optional[str],\n    actual_hmac: Optional[str],\n    reason: str,\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Build structured JSON report for --json output.\"\"\"\n    entry = entry if entry is not None else {}  # None: not about one line (line 0)\n    return {\n        \"status\": status,\n        \"line\": line_num,\n        \"reason\": reason,\n        \"entry_ts\": entry.get(\"ts\"),\n        \"entry_action\": entry.get(\"action\"),\n        \"expected_hmac\": expected_hmac,\n        \"actual_hmac\": actual_hmac,\n    }\n\n\ndef _emit_human_report(report: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Pretty-print tamper report to stderr.\"\"\"\n    sys.stderr.write(\n        \"TAMPER DETECTED at line {line}\\n\".format(line=report[\"line\"])\n    )\n    sys.stderr.write(\n        \"  entry_ts:      {ts}\\n\".format(ts=report.get(\"entry_ts\"))\n    )\n    sys.stderr.write(\n        \"  entry_action:  {a}\\n\".format(a=report.get(\"entry_action\"))\n    )\n    sys.stderr.write(\"  reason:        {r}\\n\".format(r=report.get(\"reason\")))\n    if report.get(\"expected_hmac\"):\n        sys.stderr.write(\n            \"  expected_hmac: {h}\\n\".format(h=report[\"expected_hmac\"])\n        )\n    if report.get(\"actual_hmac\"):\n        sys.stderr.write(\n            \"  actual_hmac:   {h}\\n\".format(h=report[\"actual_hmac\"])\n        )\n    sys.stderr.write(\n        \"Chain broken. Do not trust entries >= line {n}.\\n\".format(\n            n=report[\"line\"]\n        )\n    )\n\n\ndef _emit_report(report, json_output: bool) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Emit a tamper/malformed report either as JSON or human text.\"\"\"\n    if json_output:\n        print(json.dumps(report, separators=(\",\", \":\")))\n    else:\n        _emit_human_report(report)\n\n\ndef _decode_entry(\n    line_num: int, raw: str, strict_contract: bool = False,\n) -> \"tuple[Optional[str], Optional[dict], Optional[int]]\":\n    \"\"\"Parse raw line → (stripped, entry_dict or None, exit_code or None).\n\n    Returns ``(None, None, exit_code)`` on decode failure; returns\n    ``(\"\", None, None)`` for blank lines; otherwise ``(stripped, entry, None)``.\n    Under the strict contract a line that is not one JSON object raises\n    :class:`_StrictFailure` instead, so that --json still gets its one object.\n    \"\"\"\n    stripped = raw.strip()\n    if not stripped:\n        return \"\", None, None\n    if strict_contract:\n        try:\n            entry = json.loads(stripped, parse_constant=_refuse_json_constant)\n        except (ValueError, RecursionError) as e:\n            raise _StrictFailure(\n                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n                \"malformed_json_line: line {n}: {t}: {e}\".format(\n                    n=line_num, t=type(e).__name__, e=str(e)[:200]),\n            ) from e\n        if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n            raise _StrictFailure(\n                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n                \"malformed_json_line: line {n} is not a JSON object\".format(n=line_num),\n            )\n        return stripped, entry, None\n    try:\n        entry = json.loads(stripped)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n        _err(\n            \"error: line {n} is malformed JSON: {e}\".format(n=line_num, e=e)\n        )\n        return None, None, EXIT_MALFORMED\n    if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n        _err(\"error: line {n} is not a JSON object\".format(n=line_num))\n        return None, None, EXIT_MALFORMED\n    return stripped, entry, None\n\n\ndef _classify_hmac_presence(\n    state: str, entry: dict, line_num: int, json_output: bool,\n) -> \"tuple[str, Any]\":\n    \"\"\"Handle the hmac-missing vs. hmac-present fork.\n\n    Returns ``(status, payload)`` where status is one of:\n      - ``\"pre_v29\"`` — pre-v2.9 entry, skip with counter bump\n      - ``\"transition\"`` — violation: hmac-bearing → hmac-less, exit tamper\n      - ``\"malformed\"`` — hmac field wrong type/length, exit malformed\n      - ``\"ok\"`` — payload is the validated hmac_hex string\n    \"\"\"\n    hmac_hex = entry.get(\"hmac\")\n    if hmac_hex is None:\n        if state == \"CHAIN_START\":\n            return \"pre_v29\", None\n        report = _format_report(\n            \"tamper\", line_num, entry, None, None,\n            \"transition_violation: hmac-bearing entry followed by \"\n            \"hmac-less entry (one-way rule)\",\n        )\n        _emit_report(report, json_output)\n        return \"transition\", EXIT_TAMPER\n\n    if not isinstance(hmac_hex, str) or len(hmac_hex) != HMAC_HEX_LEN:\n        report = _format_report(\n            \"malformed\", line_num, entry, None, str(hmac_hex),\n            \"hmac_field_malformed: not 64 hex chars\",\n        )\n        _emit_report(report, json_output)\n        return \"malformed\", EXIT_MALFORMED\n\n    return \"ok\", hmac_hex\n\n\ndef _verify_entry_hmac(\n    key: bytes,\n    prev_hmac: bytes,\n    entry: dict,\n    hmac_hex: str,\n    line_num: int,\n    json_output: bool,\n    strict_contract: bool = False,\n) -> \"tuple[Optional[bytes], Optional[int]]\":\n    \"\"\"Recompute entry HMAC + constant-time compare against recorded.\n\n    Returns ``(new_prev_hmac, exit_code)``. On success returns\n    ``(actual_bytes, None)``; on failure returns ``(None, exit_code)``.\n    \"\"\"\n    entry_sans = {\n        k: v for k, v in entry.items()\n        if k != \"hmac\" and k != \"hmac_error\"\n    }\n    try:\n        expected = compute_entry_hmac(key, prev_hmac, entry_sans)\n    except AuditHmacError as e:\n        if strict_contract:\n            raise _StrictFailure(\n                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n                \"hmac_compute_failed: line {n}: {e}\".format(n=line_num, e=e),\n            ) from e\n        _err(\n            \"error: HMAC compute failed at line {n}: {e}\".format(\n                n=line_num, e=e\n            )\n        )\n        return None, EXIT_MALFORMED\n\n    try:\n        actual = from_hex(hmac_hex)\n    except AuditHmacError as e:\n        if strict_contract:\n            raise _StrictFailure(\n                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n                \"hmac_field_unparseable: line {n}: {e}\".format(n=line_num, e=e),\n            ) from e\n        _err(\n            \"error: hmac field not parseable at line {n}: {e}\".format(\n                n=line_num, e=e\n            )\n        )\n        return None, EXIT_MALFORMED\n\n    import hmac as _h\n    if not _h.compare_digest(expected, actual):\n        report = _format_report(\n            \"tamper\", line_num, entry,\n            expected.hex(), hmac_hex,\n            \"hmac_mismatch: recomputed does not match recorded\",\n        )\n        _emit_report(report, json_output)\n        return None, EXIT_TAMPER\n\n    return actual, None\n\n\ndef verify(\n    log_lines,\n    key: bytes,\n    since: int = 1,\n    json_output: bool = False,\n    verbose: bool = False,\n    enforce_marker_if_manifest: bool = True,\n    log_dir: Optional[Path] = None,\n    strict_against_counter: bool = False,\n    counter_override: Optional[int] = None,\n    chain_length_source: Optional[str] = None,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Walk lines; return an exit code.\n\n    ``chain_length_source`` is set only by :func:`_main_strict` and turns on the strict\n    contract of the module docstring: ``sidecar``, ``override`` or ``absent``.\n\n    ``log_lines`` is an iterable of (line_num, raw_line) tuples.\n    ``since`` is 1-indexed starting line.\n\n    Chain state machine:\n      CHAIN_START — no hmac seen yet (pre-v2.9 zone).\n      CHAIN_ACTIVE — at least one hmac seen; prev_hmac tracked.\n\n    PLAN-112-FOLLOWUP-hmac-tamper-fix Wave B.3 / ADR-055-AMEND-2:\n    If ``enforce_marker_if_manifest=True`` AND the\n    ``audit-log.rotation-manifest.json`` sidecar exists, line 1 of the\n    log MUST be an entry with ``action == \"chain_reset_marker\"``;\n    otherwise STATUS_TAMPER. Verifier uses LOCAL semantics (line 1\n    inspection + sidecar presence); does NOT walk archives.\n    \"\"\"\n    # AC12 enforcement: manifest-mode marker check on line 1. Read manifest\n    # from log's SAME directory (NOT _audit_dir_from_env) so test envs with\n    # custom log paths don't inherit production manifest state.\n    manifest_present = False\n    if enforce_marker_if_manifest and log_dir is not None:\n        try:\n            manifest_path = log_dir / audit_hmac.ROTATION_MANIFEST_FILENAME\n            manifest_present = manifest_path.exists()\n        except Exception:\n            manifest_present = False\n\n    state = \"CHAIN_START\"\n    prev_hmac = GENESIS_PREV\n    verified_count = 0\n    pre_v29_count = 0\n    first_chain_line_checked = False\n    strict_contract = chain_length_source is not None\n\n    for line_num, raw in log_lines:\n        if line_num < since:\n            continue\n\n        stripped, entry, exit_code = _decode_entry(line_num, raw, strict_contract)\n        if exit_code is not None:\n            return exit_code\n        if not stripped:\n            continue\n        assert entry is not None\n\n        status, payload = _classify_hmac_presence(\n            state, entry, line_num, json_output\n        )\n        if status == \"pre_v29\":\n            pre_v29_count += 1\n            continue\n        if status in (\"transition\", \"malformed\"):\n            return payload  # type: ignore[return-value]\n\n        hmac_hex = payload  # \"ok\" path\n        assert isinstance(hmac_hex, str)\n\n        if state == \"CHAIN_START\":\n            state = \"CHAIN_ACTIVE\"\n            prev_hmac = GENESIS_PREV\n\n        # AC12 enforcement: if rotation-manifest sidecar present, FIRST\n        # chain-active entry MUST be chain_reset_marker. Non-marker line 1\n        # in marker-required mode = STATUS_TAMPER per ADR-055-AMEND-2.\n        if (enforce_marker_if_manifest and manifest_present\n                and not first_chain_line_checked):\n            first_chain_line_checked = True\n            if entry.get(\"action\") != \"chain_reset_marker\":\n                report = _format_report(\n                    \"tamper\", line_num, entry, None, None,\n                    \"marker_required_but_absent: audit-log.rotation-manifest.json \"\n                    \"present but line 1 action is not chain_reset_marker per \"\n                    \"ADR-055-AMEND-2\",\n                )\n                _emit_report(report, json_output)\n                return EXIT_TAMPER\n\n        new_prev, exit_code = _verify_entry_hmac(\n            key, prev_hmac, entry, hmac_hex, line_num, json_output, strict_contract\n        )\n        if exit_code is not None:\n            return exit_code\n        assert new_prev is not None\n        prev_hmac = new_prev\n        verified_count += 1\n\n    # PLAN-118 AC-B9-ii — strict-against-counter tail-truncation detection.\n    # The persisted ``audit-log.chain-length`` counter is the monotonic\n    # number of HMAC-bearing entries ever written (incremented under the\n    # same FileLock as the entry itself). If the walker saw FEWER\n    # HMAC-bearing entries than the counter says, the chain tail has\n    # been truncated even though the surviving prefix verifies clean.\n    # Flag as STATUS_TAMPER with reason=chain_length_truncation.\n    if strict_against_counter:\n        try:\n            expected_length = (\n                counter_override if counter_override is not None\n                else audit_hmac.read_chain_length()\n            )\n        except Exception as e:\n            report = _format_report(\n                \"tamper\", 0, None, None, None,\n                f\"chain_length_read_failed: {type(e).__name__}: {e}\",\n            )\n            _emit_report(report, json_output)\n            return EXIT_TAMPER\n        if verified_count < expected_length:\n            report = _format_report(\n                \"tamper\", 0, None, None, None,\n                \"chain_length_truncation: walker counted {v} HMAC-bearing \"\n                \"entries, persisted counter says {n}\".format(\n                    v=verified_count, n=expected_length\n                ),\n            )\n            report[\"verified_count\"] = verified_count\n            report[\"expected_length\"] = expected_length\n            _emit_report(report, json_output)\n            return EXIT_TAMPER\n\n    summary: Dict[str, Any] = {\n        \"status\": \"intact\",\n        \"verified_count\": verified_count,\n        \"pre_v29_count\": pre_v29_count,\n    }\n    if chain_length_source is not None:\n        summary[\"chain_length_source\"] = chain_length_source\n        if not json_output and chain_length_source == \"absent\":\n            _err(\n                \"warning: chain_length_source=absent: no chain-length counter, \"\n                \"tail truncation NOT checked\"\n            )\n    if json_output:\n        print(json.dumps(summary, separators=(\",\", \":\")))\n    elif verbose:\n        sys.stderr.write(\n            \"OK: chain intact. verified={v} pre_v29={p}\\n\".format(\n                v=verified_count, p=pre_v29_count\n            )\n        )\n    return EXIT_INTACT\n\n\ndef _iter_lines(log_path: Optional[Path]) -> \"Iterator[tuple[int, str]]\":\n    \"\"\"Yield ``(line_num, raw_line)`` pairs from file or stdin.\"\"\"\n    if log_path is None:\n        for i, raw in enumerate(sys.stdin, start=1):\n            yield (i, raw)\n        return\n    if not log_path.exists():\n        _err(\"error: log file not found: {p}\".format(p=log_path))\n        sys.exit(EXIT_MALFORMED)\n    with log_path.open(\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        for i, raw in enumerate(f, start=1):\n            yield (i, raw)\n\n\n_COUNTER_RE = re.compile(r\"[0-9]{1,32}\")\n_NONBLOCK_READ = os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NONBLOCK | getattr(os, \"O_CLOEXEC\", 0)\n\n\ndef _open_regular_strict(path: Path, what: str, unreadable: str) -> \"io.BufferedReader\":\n    \"\"\"Open without blocking; refuse by fstat what is not a regular file.\n\n    The check and the read act on the same descriptor. O_NONBLOCK is why a FIFO with\n    no writer returns here instead of hanging on the open.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        fd = os.open(str(path), _NONBLOCK_READ)\n    except PermissionError as e:\n        raise _StrictFailure(\n            EXIT_PERM, STATUS_PERM_ERROR,\n            \"{w}: cannot read {p}: {e}\".format(w=unreadable, p=path, e=e),\n        ) from e\n    except OSError as e:\n        raise _StrictFailure(\n            EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n            \"{w}: cannot open {p}: {t}: {e}\".format(\n                w=unreadable, p=path, t=type(e).__name__, e=e),\n        ) from e\n    if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(fd).st_mode):\n        os.close(fd)\n        raise _StrictFailure(\n            EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n            \"{w}: {what} {p} is not a regular file\".format(w=unreadable, what=what, p=path),\n        )\n    return os.fdopen(fd, \"rb\")\n\n\ndef _expected_length_strict(counter_override: Optional[int]) -> Tuple[int, str]:\n    \"\"\"``(expected length, source)``. Unlike ``audit_hmac.read_chain_length``, an\n    illegible counter is an error (S363-4): only real absence is allowed through.\"\"\"\n    if counter_override is not None:\n        return counter_override, \"override\"\n    path = audit_hmac.chain_length_path()\n    try:\n        os.lstat(str(path))\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        return 0, \"absent\"\n    except OSError as e:\n        raise _StrictFailure(\n            EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n            \"chain_length_unreadable: cannot stat {p}: {e}\".format(p=path, e=e),\n        ) from e\n    with _open_regular_strict(path, \"counter\", \"chain_length_unreadable\") as stream:\n        raw = stream.read(64)\n    text = raw.decode(\"ascii\", \"replace\").strip(\" \\t\\r\\n\")\n    if _COUNTER_RE.fullmatch(text) is None:\n        raise _StrictFailure(\n            EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n            \"chain_length_unreadable: {p} does not hold a plain decimal count\".format(p=path),\n        )\n    return int(text), \"sidecar\"\n\n\ndef _read_key_strict(key_file: Optional[Path]) -> bytes:\n    \"\"\":func:`_read_key` with its exits and OS errors mapped to named failures.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return _read_key(key_file)\n    except SystemExit as e:\n        if e.code == EXIT_KEY_MISSING:\n            raise _StrictFailure(EXIT_KEY_MISSING, STATUS_KEY_MISSING, \"key_missing\") from e\n        raise _StrictFailure(EXIT_PERM, STATUS_PERM_ERROR, \"key_unusable\") from e\n    except OSError as e:\n        raise _StrictFailure(\n            EXIT_PERM, STATUS_PERM_ERROR, \"key_unusable: {e}\".format(e=e)\n        ) from e\n\n\ndef _open_log_strict(log_path: Optional[Path]) -> \"io.TextIOWrapper\":\n    \"\"\"One decoding path for file and stdin, so the same bytes get the same verdict.\"\"\"\n    if log_path is None:\n        return io.TextIOWrapper(sys.stdin.buffer, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n    try:\n        os.lstat(str(log_path))\n    except FileNotFoundError as e:\n        raise _StrictFailure(\n            EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n            \"log_not_found: {p}\".format(p=log_path),\n        ) from e\n    except OSError:\n        pass  # the open below names it\n    binary = _open_regular_strict(log_path, \"log\", \"log_not_regular\")\n    return io.TextIOWrapper(binary, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n\n\ndef _main_strict(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    \"\"\"The --strict-against-counter contract of the module docstring.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        log_path = _resolve_log_path(args)\n        if log_path is _LOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED:\n            raise _StrictFailure(\n                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n                \"log_unresolved: cannot resolve default audit-log path; pass --log-file\",\n            )\n        key = _read_key_strict(args.key_file)\n        expected, source = _expected_length_strict(args.counter_override)\n        stream = _open_log_strict(log_path)\n        try:\n            return verify(\n                enumerate(stream, start=1),\n                key,\n                since=args.since,\n                json_output=args.json,\n                verbose=args.verbose,\n                log_dir=log_path.parent if log_path is not None else None,\n                strict_against_counter=True,\n                counter_override=expected,\n                chain_length_source=source,\n            )\n        finally:\n            stream.close()\n    except _StrictFailure as failure:\n        return _strict_emit(failure, args.json)\n    except UnicodeError as e:\n        return _strict_emit(\n            _StrictFailure(\n                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n                \"log_undecodable: {t}: {e}\".format(t=type(e).__name__, e=str(e)[:200]),\n            ),\n            args.json,\n        )\n    except Exception as e:  # the CLI's boundary: named and fail-closed, no traceback\n        return _strict_emit(\n            _StrictFailure(\n                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n                \"internal_error: {t}: {e}\".format(t=type(e).__name__, e=str(e)[:200]),\n            ),\n            args.json,\n        )\n\n\nclass _PreScanFailed(Exception):\n    \"\"\"The lenient pre-scan could not read the argv.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass _PreScanParser(argparse.ArgumentParser):\n    \"\"\"Only learns whether this is a strict run; never reports anything itself.\"\"\"\n\n    def error(self, message: str) -> Any:\n        raise _PreScanFailed(message)\n\n\nclass _ContractParser(argparse.ArgumentParser):\n    \"\"\"argparse, except that under strict an argument error is a named rc 3.\"\"\"\n\n    strict_json: Optional[bool] = None  # None: not strict, stock behaviour\n\n    def error(self, message: str) -> Any:\n        if self.strict_json is None:\n            super().error(message)\n        raise SystemExit(\n            _strict_emit(\n                _StrictFailure(\n                    EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n                    \"invalid_arguments: \" + message,\n                ),\n                self.strict_json,\n            )\n        )\n\n\ndef _strict_prescan(argv: List[str]) -> Tuple[bool, bool, Optional[str]]:\n    \"\"\"``(strict, json, raw override)``, before argparse validates or prints help.\n\n    The same options as the real parser (abbreviations stay as ambiguous as they are\n    there) without its value types. An argv the scan cannot read falls back to looking\n    for the two flags by token.\n    \"\"\"\n    pre = _add_arguments(_PreScanParser(add_help=False), lenient=True)\n    try:\n        known, _ = pre.parse_known_args(argv)\n    except _PreScanFailed:\n        def has(flag: str, floor: str) -> bool:\n            return any(t.startswith(floor) and flag.startswith(t) for t in argv)\n        return (\n            has(\"--strict-against-counter\", \"--str\"),\n            has(\"--json\", \"--j\"),\n            None,\n        )\n    return known.strict_against_counter, known.json, known.counter_override\n\n\n_LOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED = Path(\"/nonexistent/ceo-audit-log-unresolved\")\n\n\ndef _resolve_log_path(args: argparse.Namespace) -> Optional[Path]:\n    \"\"\"The log path of ``args``: None means stdin. :data:`_LOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED` means\n    the default directory could not be resolved.\"\"\"\n    if args.stdin or (args.log_file is not None and str(args.log_file) == \"-\"):\n        return None\n    if args.log_file is not None:\n        return args.log_file\n    env_log = os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH\")\n    if env_log:\n        return Path(env_log)\n    # Default: sibling of audit-key resolution.\n    try:\n        default_dir = audit_hmac._audit_dir_from_env()\n    except Exception:\n        return _LOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED\n    return default_dir / \"audit-log.jsonl\"\n\n\ndef _add_arguments(parser: Any, lenient: bool = False) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"Declare the CLI. ``lenient`` leaves the two int values unconverted (pre-scan).\"\"\"\n    int_type = str if lenient else int\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--log-file\",\n        type=Path,\n        default=None,\n        help=\"Path to audit-log.jsonl (default: resolved via env / stdin)\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--key-file\",\n        type=Path,\n        default=None,\n        help=\"Path to audit-key (default: resolved via env)\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--since\",\n        type=int_type,\n        default=1,\n        help=\"1-indexed starting line (default: 1 = verify from genesis)\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--json\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"Emit structured JSON report to stdout\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--verbose\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"Print 'OK' summary on success (default: silent success)\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--stdin\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"Read log from stdin (equivalent to --log-file -)\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--strict-against-counter\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=(\n            \"PLAN-118 AC-B9 — additionally enforce \"\n            \"verified_count >= audit-log.chain-length (tail-truncation \"\n            \"detection). Without this flag, a truncated tail whose \"\n            \"surviving prefix verifies clean would be reported intact.\"\n        ),\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--counter-override\",\n        type=int_type,\n        default=None,\n        help=(\n            \"Test/forensic-only: override the persisted \"\n            \"audit-log.chain-length counter (paired with \"\n            \"--strict-against-counter). Default reads the on-disk sidecar.\"\n        ),\n    )\n    return parser\n\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"CLI entrypoint — verify an audit-log HMAC chain end-to-end.\"\"\"\n    args_in = list(sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv)\n    strict, strict_json, raw_override = _strict_prescan(args_in)\n    if strict and raw_override is not None and _COUNTER_RE.fullmatch(raw_override) is None:\n        return _strict_emit(\n            _StrictFailure(\n                EXIT_MALFORMED, STATUS_MALFORMED,\n                \"counter_override_invalid: expected plain decimal digits\",\n            ),\n            strict_json,\n        )\n    parser = _ContractParser(\n        description=\"Verify the HMAC chain in audit-log.jsonl.\",\n        epilog=\"Exit 0=intact, 1=tamper, 2=key missing, 3=malformed, 4=perm.\",\n    )\n    if strict:\n        parser.strict_json = strict_json\n    args = _add_arguments(parser).parse_args(args_in)\n    if args.strict_against_counter:\n        return _main_strict(args)\n\n    # Resolve log path.\n    log_path = _resolve_log_path(args)\n    if log_path is _LOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED:\n        _err(\"error: cannot resolve default audit-log path; \"\n             \"pass --log-file\")\n        return EXIT_MALFORMED\n\n    # Read key.\n    try:\n        key = _read_key(args.key_file)\n    except SystemExit:\n        raise\n\n    return verify(\n        _iter_lines(log_path),\n        key,\n        since=args.since,\n        json_output=args.json,\n        verbose=args.verbose,\n        log_dir=log_path.parent if hasattr(log_path, \"parent\") else None,\n    )\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":854,"startLine":1,"totalLines":854}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Em1fpvsJqAVJufhdxYXbXg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
