{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NeiJ4SWSG1RgwcQSr1cyNL","type":"tool_result","content":"165:def _audit_dir_from_env() -> Path:\n166-    \"\"\"Resolve the audit dir, aligned with audit_emit._audit_dir().\n167-\n168-    Precedence mirrors audit_emit + spool_writer so the HMAC sidecars\n169-    (key, last-hmac, chain-length) co-locate with the audit log + its\n170-    FileLock under the coherent-env contract (processes writing one log\n171-    share the same CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR, or all run pure-$HOME):\n172-\n173-      ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH`` parent (the EFFECTIVE log — most specific,\n174-      rail r2 D) -> ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` -> ``CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR`` ->\n175-      the single family resolver (``_lib/runtime_paths``, PLAN-182 W1:\n176-      ``$HOME/.claude/projects/<native-slug>/``).\n177-\n178-    Honoring CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR closes a latent split (S168): a LOG_DIR-only\n179-    process resolved its FileLock under LOG_DIR but its chain-length counter\n180-    under $HOME, so two such processes (same $HOME, different LOG_DIR)\n181-    shared one counter while holding different locks — a lost counter\n182-    increment that weakens tail-truncation detection.\n183-    \"\"\"\n184-    # PLAN-182 W1 rail r2 D: a familia segue o LOG EFETIVO — PATH (mais\n185-    # especifico) vence DIR, igual a audit_emit._log_path/_log_family_dir,\n186-    # spool_writer e audit_log. Com AMBOS setados, log+lock+key+sidecars\n187-    # ficam TODOS no parent do PATH; a ordem antiga (DIR primeiro) partia\n188-    # a familia em dois diretorios.\n189-    p = os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH\")\n190-    log_dir = os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR\")\n--\n255:def key_path() -> Path:\n256-    \"\"\"Return the resolved audit-key path (sibling of audit-log.jsonl).\"\"\"\n257-    override = os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_KEY_PATH\")\n258-    if override:\n259-        return Path(override)\n260-    return _audit_dir_from_env() / KEY_FILENAME\n261-\n262-\n2